       +z = window face (the two rounded windows at the ends), -z = mounting boss (x +-42, z down to -44.5; the thin pieces below it,
       z -73..-112, are loose leftovers of the cones). The window face looks along the tool (mesh +z = flange +x), the boss points back at
       the wrist, the long axis lies along flange y. The plate behind the boss (flange x 0.088..0.098) sits right in front of the J6 flange
       face (x 0.09) and carries it 0.04..0.138 off the tool axis; the body (flange z 0.07..0.138, x 0.123..0.184) clears the gripper / extension (r 0.04).
       Mass is an estimate (3 kg, box inertia of the housing). Collision = boxes (housing, boss, plate): the STL has 420k triangles.
